e used/is permitted in this environment. Given I'm a subagent, maybe I need to check if the main agent has permissions to use me, or if there are restrictions.\n\nWait, looking more carefully at the context: The user message is \"[Tue 2026-02-10 17:44 UTC] Test if this model is allowed.\" This is the user's message, not the main agent's instruction to me as a subagent. The user might be asking me (the assistant) to test if a model is allowed. But I'm currently in a subagent session created for that specific purpose according to the subagent context.\n\nThe subagent context says: \"You are a subagent spawned by the main agent for a specific task. Complete this task. That's your entire purpose.\" and \"What you were created to handle: Test if this model is allowed.\"\n\nSo the main agent created me to handle the task \"Test if this model is allowed.\" This is likely a test or check. I need to determine what \"allowed\" means in this context. It could be about:\n- Tool access permissions\n- Model restrictions\n- Whether the model is on an approved list\n- Something else\n\nGiven I have access to tools like read, write, exec, browser, etc., maybe I need to verify that these are indeed allowed and report back.\n\nAlternatively, maybe \"this model\" refers to a specific model name. The runtime shows the model being used: \"model=openrouter/stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free | default_model=moonshotai/kimi-k2.5\". So perhaps I need to check if these models are allowed in the system.\n\nI think the best approach is to:\n1. Check if there's any configuration that defines allowed models or restrictions\n2. Try using some tools to see if they work\n3. Report my findings\n\nGiven I'm a subagent, I should focus on the task and produce a concise report. I should not ask the user for clarification; I'm supposed to complete the task.\n\nLet me start by looking for any configuration files that might define model allowlists or permissions. I'll check the workspace for files like:\n- AGENTS.md (already loaded, might have policy)\n- TOOLS.md (already loaded)\n- Any other configuration\n\nActually, the AGENTS.md and TOOLS.md were provided in the subagent context. They seem to be general guidelines for the assistant, not specific restrictions on models.\n\nMaybe I need to check the OpenClaw configuration or something in the system. However, my tools are limited to those listed in the \"Tool availability\" section.\n\nGiven the ambiguity, I should interpret the task as: \"Determine whether the current model (the one I'm running as) is permitted to operate within this environment.\" And since I'm already running and have tool access, the answer is likely \"yes, it is allowed.\" But I need to verify.\n\nPerhaps the test is to see if I can access certain restricted operations or if there are any policy filters.\n\nLet me think about what would indicate a model is \"not allowed\":\n- Tools are disabled\n- Certain commands are blocked\n- There's an explicit denylist\n- The system prevents execution\n\nSince I have access to a broad set of tools and I'm executing, it seems allowed. But maybe there's a specific check I need to perform.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the task is to test if a model (like step-3.5-flash) is allowed to be used by OpenClaw. Possibly there's a configuration file that lists allowed models. I could search for such a file.\n\nGiven the workspace is /root/.openclaw/workspace, I can explore that directory. But I need to be careful: I'm a subagent, so my actions are limited to the tools I have, which include reading files, executing commands, etc. I can use exec to run commands to search for configuration files.\n\nLet's start by exploring the workspace structure. I'll use exec to list files and read relevant configurations.\n\nPlan:\n1. List files in workspace to see what's there\n2. Look for config files that might define allowed models or tool policies\n3. Check if there's any explicit allow/deny list\n4. Try a simple tool call to confirm tools work\n5. Report findings\n\nI'll start with exec to see the workspace structure.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll test if the current model is allowed by checking tool availability and attempting basic operations."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-f2fc106ff2f04f62a026dc6d28d0181b","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"ls -la /root/.openclaw/workspace"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":8215,"output":2861,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":11076,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770745498504}}
